    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "e59b92d8-d965-3d98-a313-7106d8024006",
                "word": "transhuman",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "12d6859c-97ea-4ba2-9fef-4e4ee1a9cb86",
                        "entry_id": "e59b92d8-d965-3d98-a313-7106d8024006",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more transhuman"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "446dfbb2-080a-4741-9111-25d870c346a9",
                        "entry_id": "e59b92d8-d965-3d98-a313-7106d8024006",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most transhuman"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "95ac9476-a7b2-39cd-8a00-fcfb7d019c03",
                        "entry_id": "e59b92d8-d965-3d98-a313-7106d8024006",
                        "glosses": [
                            "More than human; superhuman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "570b5c24-4967-4eb6-a3c8-7dd489af933d",
                                "sense_id": "95ac9476-a7b2-39cd-8a00-fcfb7d019c03",
                                "text": "Turning fallible human foot soldiers into transhuman machines who need neither sleep nor food, and are incapable of resistance and independent thought, is a Napoleonic dream ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "890ebab3-b99e-4d1b-8f99-b980b3614435",
                                "sense_id": "95ac9476-a7b2-39cd-8a00-fcfb7d019c03",
                                "text": "A template for those who will become transhuman."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e2cbca88-b117-3d75-b1b3-b343f12d9a86",
                        "entry_id": "e59b92d8-d965-3d98-a313-7106d8024006",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Related to transhumanism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ff9dde5-30fe-4c2a-9910-1870cb48cb13",
                                "sense_id": "e2cbca88-b117-3d75-b1b3-b343f12d9a86",
                                "text": "I believe that this is important, because taken in isolation the kind of enhancements portrayed by transhuman philosophers might seem relatively innocuous."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4d677d8-7765-45cb-804f-421dbf3b3ad8",
                                "sense_id": "e2cbca88-b117-3d75-b1b3-b343f12d9a86",
                                "text": "The transhuman ideal is based upon a reconception of evolution, a perfecting and transcending of the human race through the next step in progress: not through biological mutation but through science and technology."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "316b3256-eeb5-48db-83c5-d7ba440bc2b3",
                                "sense_id": "e2cbca88-b117-3d75-b1b3-b343f12d9a86",
                                "text": "In a study of transhumanists and video games, fully twothirds of the participants claimed that video games incline players toward a transhuman sense of self."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "678b010c-1e96-35af-8d28-249a54b5d96d",
                        "entry_id": "e59b92d8-d965-3d98-a313-7106d8024006",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Involving something beyond the merely human; transcending human limitations or boundaries."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed1cbbd8-f1bd-4916-b127-ffa124e38d26",
                                "sense_id": "678b010c-1e96-35af-8d28-249a54b5d96d",
                                "text": "Near-synonym: posthuman (sometimes synonymous)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa5fd4b3-b33a-479a-83a4-065139b9f633",
                                "sense_id": "678b010c-1e96-35af-8d28-249a54b5d96d",
                                "text": "This \"other world\" is transcendent because the experience of the sacred—an encounter with a reality transcending immanent life—gives birth to the idea that there are absolute, that is, transhuman, realities."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d30217bb-decf-4efb-8c10-b1be7a85afa5",
                                "sense_id": "678b010c-1e96-35af-8d28-249a54b5d96d",
                                "text": "Thus, regardless of whether one prefers to replace the father symbol with other human symbols like mother and maternal—or with transhuman and transsexual symbols like first/last reality—none of these images or symbols are really integral to the message of the Gospels."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "35694658-6318-40bf-a53a-e28186cbe463",
                                "sense_id": "678b010c-1e96-35af-8d28-249a54b5d96d",
                                "text": "Subjectivity, as a paradoxically transhuman phenomenon of awareness renderred only in ecologies, is rendered into inscriptions and images even as no self is adequate to the report."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "ab35cedd-e779-3ab6-9bc1-7f54dae56420",
                "word": "transhuman",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "93b3d721-9b44-4894-9b16-42d6b2e7840a",
                        "entry_id": "ab35cedd-e779-3ab6-9bc1-7f54dae56420",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "transhumans"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e90890b5-facc-3983-9ac1-57b38379a6ab",
                        "entry_id": "ab35cedd-e779-3ab6-9bc1-7f54dae56420",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An enhanced human:",
                            "An individual having characteristics transitional between a human and a posthuman species."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9616f77-e03c-4178-ab4b-ac5a449f469f",
                                "sense_id": "e90890b5-facc-3983-9ac1-57b38379a6ab",
                                "text": "In the same way that a transhuman is a transitional human, Christians are also humans in transition, living in a kingdom that has come and yet is coming, “strangers in the world.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b336747d-c87a-36d6-8637-b22c51e04c4e",
                        "entry_id": "ab35cedd-e779-3ab6-9bc1-7f54dae56420",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An enhanced human:",
                            "An individual of a posthuman species."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebee2844-e9e7-43f3-bb5c-cc1afba0f59f",
                                "sense_id": "b336747d-c87a-36d6-8637-b22c51e04c4e",
                                "text": "On the coffee table rested a sculpture of the fundamental, recombinant DNA of the present transhumans."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ccb7f1e6-61b6-4bc8-a02f-c679d265ba5a",
                                "sense_id": "b336747d-c87a-36d6-8637-b22c51e04c4e",
                                "text": "In practice, this technological transhumation would wreak havoc on the earth. While modern transhumans are meant to come into being through technology, Augustine offers two models of transhumans made by a divine rather than a human creator -- Adam and Eve in Eden and the resurrected saints in heaven."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2544c5c-e412-46a6-a8a5-c000a85c0b21",
                                "sense_id": "b336747d-c87a-36d6-8637-b22c51e04c4e",
                                "text": "Will it happen again if we transition from human to transhuman?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c06d3114-12ee-333a-a034-998accb9eaa5",
                        "entry_id": "ab35cedd-e779-3ab6-9bc1-7f54dae56420",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A being that transcends humanity; a superhuman being."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0508d7d6-c3f4-4648-bae8-dbd4be7ea9c4",
                                "sense_id": "c06d3114-12ee-333a-a034-998accb9eaa5",
                                "text": "I bet every critter that thinks it thinks—even the transhumans—worry about how to do right for themselves and the ones they love."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "451bee0b-78c5-4161-995c-2c44c684fbdf",
                                "sense_id": "c06d3114-12ee-333a-a034-998accb9eaa5",
                                "text": "Imagine a living computer running a simulation where math functions within the simulation think. Then consider an implication of anthrocosmology: if human consciousness created reality and transhumans can simulate any reality they can imagine, that suggest the physical universe has no special status above any other virtual reality."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c9a2fc6-7c8e-44b1-9cad-8e88f72a7811",
                                "sense_id": "c06d3114-12ee-333a-a034-998accb9eaa5",
                                "text": "Now ask yourself a question, don't these transhumans have as much a right in killing us for food as we do in killing cows?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
